{"id": "z1144", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "To improve health, a good strategy would be D, a spa trip. Spa trips often include activities like massage s, yoga, and other relaxation techniques that can reduce stress, improve mental well-be ing, and promote overall wellness.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1152", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A meadow vole needs to eat bug s after giving birth. So the correct answer is C, bugs.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1160", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The sidewalk next to a house with a crack and vegetation growing from it is considered erosion. Erosion happens when natural forces like water, wind, or temperature changes break down the material over time. In this case, the cracks in the sidewalk allow plants to grow through, which is a sign of gradual breakdown caused by environmental factors. So the correct answer is D, e rosion.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1168", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "C, a trip to the moon. It is the closest option listed and can be reached within days using current spacecraft technology. Mars takes several months due to distance, while the northern star is so far away it's not practical for human travel with today' s tech. So the answer is C.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1176", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The appropriate place to put the used motor oil is in a recycling bin. It should be taken to an authorized collection center because it contains harmful chemicals that can contaminate soil and water if not handled properly.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1184", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Polar bears live in frosty environments. So the correct answer is A, frosty environment s. They are well adapted to cold climates like the Arctic where they hunt seals on sea ice.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1192", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, it was not invented by Thomas Ed ison. The process of past orization was developed much earlier than Edison's time. It was actually discovered independently by Louis Pasteur in France and Joseph Li ster in England around the mid-19th century. So while Edison made significant contributions to technology, he did not invent past orization.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1200", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C, heat. While both incandescent and LED bulbs can produce white light, the key difference lies in how they generate it. In candescent bulb s create light by passing electric current through a filament, which heats up until it glows. This process results in a significant amount of energy being wasted as heat. In contrast, LED bulb s use semiconductor s to directly convert electricity into light with minimal heat production. Therefore, the main difference between them is the amount of heat generated during operation.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 30, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1208", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A food that is a source of heat would be ramen. It's typically served hot and provides warmth.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1216", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The special tissues in plants that transport mineral s throughout the plant are similar to a wick.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1224", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The respiratory system transfer s oxygen to the circ ulatory system. So the answer is D. O.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1232", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If a new species of predator joins a community, the most likely outcome is that prey will experience a drop in population. This happens because the new predator will hunt the existing prey, increasing pressure on their numbers. While it's possible for pre y populations to eventually stabilize or even rebound over time, initially they usually decline due to the added pred ation. The other options are less likely; predators don' t typically switch to herbivory without significant changes in diet, and while some old species might be affected, extinction isn't guaranteed just from a new predator joining. So the best answer is C: prey will experience a drop in population.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 31, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1240", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A plant that gets extra minerals such as zinc is probably placed in good soil. Good soil usually has the right balance of nutrient s, including zinc, which plants need to grow healthy. So the answer is C.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1248", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The answer is B. Its appearance. Stick bugs use their camouflage to blend in with twigs and branches, making it hard for predators to spot them.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1256", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The answer is A.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 2, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1264", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Hand dryers are designed to blow hot air, which can actually warm things up rather than cool them down. So they wouldn't be good for keeping cold drinks cool. They're also not meant for drying out clothes after rain; that's usually done with a dryer or by hanging the clothes outside. Hy drating your face and hands is the opposite of what a hand dryer does, so that doesn't work either. The best option here is D, making a damp rag damp er. If you wet a cloth and then blow on it with a hand dryer, the fast air can help spread moisture quickly across a surface, kind of like a mini dampener effect.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 32, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1272", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A fallen leaf, a will turn into a tree. b will become bright green. c will begin to recycle the nutrients that made up its structure. d is likely to continue to grow. The correct answer is C. When leaves fall off trees in autumn, they begin to break down and decompose. This process releases nutrient s back into the soil. These nutrients are then absorbed by other plants, helping them grow. So, the fallen leaf starts recycling its own materials to support new growth in the ecosystem.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1280", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "You can experience a change of pressure when B, so aring the skies. As you go higher into the sky, the air pressure drop s significantly. This is why airplane s have pressurized cabin s and why your ears might pop during takeoff or landing.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1288", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Lightning can lead to A, damage to local foliage. When lightning strikes, it can cause fires or burn plants and trees in the area, leading to visible damage to vegetation. While rain bows might appear after a storm, they are not caused by lightning itself.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1296", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Which of the following human activities can lead to a change in the local ecosystem? swimming in a lake, B. building a new subdivision, C. dancing in a field, D. going for a hike. The answer is B. building a new sub division. This activity involves clearing land, constructing buildings, and changing the landscape, which directly impacts habitats and disrupt s natural ecosystems. In contrast, swimming in a lake, dancing in a field, or hiking are generally low-impact activities that do not significantly alter the environment unless done on a massive scale.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 37, "carrier_ended": null}
