{"id": "z2048", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B. It has an all- or-nothing quality; it either happens or it does not. When a neuron fires, it does so in an all-or-none manner known as the action potential. If the membrane potential reaches the threshold, the neuron will fire fully, but if it doesn't reach that level, no action potential occurs at all. This is different from A, which suggest s a gradual process, and C, which implies diminishing strength, both of which are incorrect. D is also wrong because firing can happen anywhere along the axon depending on the input received.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 32, "carrier_ended": null}
