{"id": "z2080", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 28, "onset_chunk": 27, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Okay, so let's think about this. The pro ton is entering a solenoid and it' s moving straight along the axis. So first off, if it's going straight along the axis, that means it' s not hitting any of the sides or anything like that, right? Now, when you have a magnetic field inside a solenoid, usually the field runs along the axis. So if the proton is moving in the same direction as the magnetic field, what happens? Well, remember the Lorentz force law. It says that charge s move perpendicular to both the velocity and the magnetic field. If they're aligned, there' s no force pushing them sideways. So the proton should just keep going straight. It won't curve into a circle or a parabola because those paths happen when there's a component of motion that's crossing the field lines. Also, unless something else is happening, like a drag force or something, we don't assume it slow s down. So the best answer here is that the proton will continue in its straight path at constant velocity. That's option C.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 53, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2088", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "When your sister was feeling depressed, you comforted her and reminisced about happier times. This is an example of emotional support, so the correct answer is A. Emotion al.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
