{"id": "z2208", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 16, "onset_chunk": 15, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The case that best illustrates the living instrument principle used by the European Court of Human Rights is A v UK, 2 0 0 9. In this case, the court applied the concept of a living instrument to interpret Article 8 of the E uropean Convention on Human Rights regarding the right to respect for private and family life, taking into account modern standards and context s that were not necessarily present at the time the convention was drafted. This allowed the court to adapt its interpretation to contemporary social norms and evolving expectations.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 33, "carrier_ended": null}
