{"id": "z2224", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "During the time an aircraft produces a so nic boom, the aircraft is flying faster than sound. A sonic boom occurs when an aircraft break s the sound barrier, which means it' s traveling at or above the speed of sound. So while options like breaking the sound barrier and flying fast er than sound are related to producing a boom, the key point is that the aircraft must be moving faster than sound for the boom to happen.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
