{"id": "z2248", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 28, "onset_chunk": 28, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So the statement that is not true is B, nuclear binding energies have about the same magnitude as chemical bond energies. That' s incorrect because nu clear binding energies are much larger than chemical bond energies. Nucle ar binding energies typically range from a few hundred kilo electronvol ts to several million kilo electronvol ts per nucleon, whereas chemical bond energies are usually on the order of a few electronvolts per atom. So they're many orders of magnitude apart in scale.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
